+/// The size of a pooled block, at most the device's `maxMemoryAllocationSize`. pdx203: 16 MiB,
+/// not 64. The render server's GPU memory is a 768 MiB pool the boot loader reserves and a 1 GiB
+/// address window, both shared with Turnip's own buffers. As apps opened (usb-144) its pooled
+/// blocks held 448 MiB with 215 placed and 80 MiB more kept empty, while every block a pool made
+/// was 64 MiB and every buffer up to 32 MiB shared one; the window filled and Turnip wrote a
+/// command stream that could not grow past its end. Past half of a 16 MiB block a buffer takes
+/// memory of its own size, and a pool's slack and kept empty blocks are a quarter as large.
+pub(super) const BLOCK_BYTES: u64 = 16 << 20;
 
